  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q2-content",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=ax^2+3x+1$. Find the value of $a$ if $f'(2)=11$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=2$. From first principles, $f'(x)=2ax+3$; hence $4a+3=11$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{a(x+h)^2+3(x+h)+1-(ax^2+3x+1)}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{2axh+ah^2+3h}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}(2ax+ah+3)\\\\f'(x)&=2ax+3\\\\f'(2)&=4a+3=11\\\\4a&=8\\\\a&=2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 70
  },
